Package: Calibre
Title: FDR-Calibrated CRE-Gene Link Inference from Multiome Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Chenxin", "Jiang", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "cflorajiang@g.ucla.edu")
Author: Chenxin Jiang [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Chenxin Jiang <cflorajiang@g.ucla.edu>
Description: Provides computationally efficient, FDR-calibrated inference of
    cis-regulatory element (CRE)-gene links from single-cell multiome data.
    Calibre fits Poisson generalized linear models by default, with negative
    binomial models available as an alternative, while adjusting for
    user-specified technical and biological covariates. Synthetic null data are
    generated by standardized Pearson-residual resampling, and observed and
    null test statistics are combined to calibrate discovery thresholds for
    false discovery rate control. The package supports cell-type-specific,
    differential, and pseudotime-dynamic CRE-gene link inference.
